@1 = ~Unicorn Grove: Sirian, an elven bard, warned us that the unicorns are unusually skittish. He says their unease began when a hermit named Eaglehorn found a strange shard. Eaglehorn lives in a hut in the north-eastern part of the grove; Sirian suggested we speak with him.~

@400 = ~I must warn you: tread carefully through these woods. The unicorns have been especially uneasy of late, ever since Eaglehorn found that strange shard.~
@401 = ~Who is Eaglehorn?~
@402 = ~What shard do you mean?~
@403 = ~I have never seen a unicorn before. They are such majestic creatures.~
@404 = ~Thanks for the warning.~
@405 = ~What else would you like to know?~
@406 = ~Who is Eaglehorn?~
@407 = ~What shard do you mean?~
@408 = ~I have never seen a unicorn before. They are such majestic creatures.~
@409 = ~Thanks for the warning.~
@410 = ~He is a hermit who lives in the north-eastern part of the forest. Follow the path to the right, and you will find his hut. If you are curious, he can explain more than I can.~
@411 = ~A couple of moons ago, a band of orcish raiders made it dangerously close to the grove. They came to slaughter the unicorns for their horns, but we stopped them. We found a mysterious shard on their leader, and ever since, strange things have begun to happen.~
@412 = ~The shard is imbued with magic, yet no spell we possess can identify it. It resists our divinations, and worse, it seems to give off a dark vibration that permeates the forest. The unicorns grow ever more frightened, and something in the air has changed. It is as though the whole wood is holding its breath.~
@413 = ~I am sure Eaglehorn can explain more. What else would you like to know?~
@414 = ~Who is Eaglehorn?~
@415 = ~What shard do you mean?~
@416 = ~I have never seen a unicorn before. They are such majestic creatures.~
@417 = ~Thanks for the warning.~
@418 = ~Certainly. Stay safe, and do not try to touch the unicorns.~
@419 = ~Yes. To our people, unicorns are sacred guardians, symbols of purity and living ties to the divine and sylvan forces of nature. They keep corruption, evil, and wickedness at bay.~
@420 = ~They are so beautiful. Uncle Quayle told me stories about unicorns, but I thought he made them up to cheer me. And yet... they look just as he described them. I wonder if he truly saw one, as he always claimed.~
@421 = ~Unicorns are sacred to the elves, and they are peaceful creatures. If this shard makes them afraid, we should investigate. There is little in nature that can frighten them.~
@422 = ~Glorious creatures. Can they be ridden?~
@423 = ~Watch yourself, Anomen. Unicorns are not toys, and they will not remain friendly if you show them disrespect in their own domain.~
@424 = ~Surface elves weep and write poetry about these beasts, yet all I see is a horse with a very expensive silver spike upon its forehead.~
@425 = ~It suits your overly enthusiastic fairy-tale tastes, mage. Does it not?~
@426 = ~Shut up, Viconia. I do find them... surreal, and serene. That does not mean I have to listen to your insults.~
@427 = ~Oh? You are growing a horn of your own, just like your kindred creature. How marvellous.~
@428 = ~A living shard of Arcadia itself, trotting across the dust of this mundane prime world. See how its horn pierces the canopy like a needle of pure starlight? A tragedy in motion: impossibly pure, fiercely proud, and yet bound to the same slow dance of decay as the rest of us.~
@429 = ~Let us not invade their space. We should show our respect and ensure our presence does not disturb the delicate balance they keep. They are peaceful creatures, but peace must be respected.~
@430 = ~Bah! A bloody horned horse trots in and ye all lose yer miserable minds like it's the second comin' of Yondalla! Grow some stones, ye soft-headed runts! This is a golden trade chance starin' us right in the maw. We hack the beast down, rip out its horn, and sell it to some pointy-hat wizard for a mountain of coin, ye hear?~
@431 = ~The dwarf is correct. The alchemical properties of a unicorn's horn are exceedingly valuable in advanced incantations! Cease gawping at the beast like underdeveloped gibbons and do what you uncultured sycophants do best: butcher it. (Before I am forced to disintegrate it myself and leave you all penniless.)~
@432 = ~You... you are so cruel. <CHARNAME>, we are not going to kill them, are we?~
@433 = ~By Silvanus' might! This group is full of brutes and savages. Sometimes I wonder how we have come this far. We are NOT killing a unicorn, and if any of you so much as lay one filthy finger on one, I shall take action. Action you will not forget.~
@434 = ~Cheer up, lass. Just a jest. Nothin' wrong with that. Just put a cork in it, and you'll live longer.~
@435 = ~Watch yourself, Korgan. You have been useful so far, but there may come a time when your usefulness ends. Or when you make a mistake that forces me to do something truly cruel.~
@436 = ~Korgan, if you respect me as you have claimed, you will not lift your axe against these creatures. Am I clear?~
@437 = ~Grrr... bah! Ye... ye have me word, lass. I'll keep me axe holstered this once... but only for ye. Don't go makin' a bleedin' habit of askin' it, mind ye.~
@438 = ~Boo is as amazed as the day he met me! We have seen many wondrous creatures on our journeys, my friend, but every new encounter brings another surprise.~
@439 = ~The unicorn is a noble and sacred creature of the light, a symbol of purity in a world already choked by darkness. Never in my life have I seen one. I am glad to have witnessed such a sight before my retirement.~
@440 = ~We had better investigate. Whatever is making these unicorns so uneasy gives me little reason for optimism.~
@441 = ~The wingless wonder loses her head again over a herd of magical horses. What else is new?~
@442 = ~What would you know of splendour, Dorn? Your life is an endless procession of killings, often for no reason. I cannot imagine you appreciating the beauty of nature.~
@443 = ~Pah. This is a cold and scornful world.~
@444 = ~Your misanthropic views are sad. What would this world be without a glimpse of beauty, kindness and warmth. We'd grow up in a world full of slavery and corruption.~
@445 = ~Wake up, girl! We already live in a world of slavery and corruption. Need I remind you that your wings were cut off, or that you were imprisoned in a cage? I rose above suffering. I do not need to embrace the weakness you call beauty.~
@446 = ~I admit that magic rarely appeals to me, but I can make an exception here, especially when these creatures are forces of good.~
@447 = ~I dreamed of seeing a unicorn one day. Winthrop's stories about them sounded like fairy tales, but a girl could always dream. If I could tell him I had seen one with my own eyes, he would melt on the spot. I miss him.~
@448 = ~I know, Imoen. I miss him too. Perhaps we can visit him again one day.~
@449 = ~I cannot say I do. I barely spoke to him. You were his bigger headache.~
@450 = ~Maybe when all this is over and we recover what we have lost, we can go back to Candlekeep. After everything we have seen, that place seems so small.~
@451 = ~Yeah, you are right. We both fooled around, but he was the one endlessly trying to teach me better. Enough remembering the old days. We should keep going and solve this unicorn problem together, shall we?~
@452 = ~I dreamed of seeing a unicorn one day. Winthrop's stories about them sounded like fairy tales, but a girl could always dream. If I could tell him I had seen one with my own eyes, he would melt on the spot. I miss him.~
@453 = ~I know, Imoen. I miss him too. Perhaps we can visit him again one day.~
@454 = ~I cannot say I do. I barely spoke to him. You were his bigger headache.~
@455 = ~Maybe when all this is over and we recover what we have lost, we can go back to Candlekeep. After everything we have seen, that place seems so small.~
@456 = ~Yeah, you are right. We both fooled around, but he was the one endlessly trying to teach me better. Enough remembering the old days. We should keep going and solve this unicorn problem together, shall we?~
@457 = ~Just take care when you approach them. They are nervous, as I said, and I would not gamble on whether they will react calmly or aggressively.~
@458 = ~(The unicorn looks towards you, then turns its gaze away. You decide to give it space rather than attempt to pet it. These creatures are as perceptive as they are proud, and provoking one would be unwise.)~
